      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Iowa?",
      "a": "The state has received $1.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal government issued 19,029 awards in Iowa with an average award size of $71.3K, and obligations fell 62.3% year over year. FY-by-FY totals show FY25 at $3.6B and FY26 at $1.4B, noting that FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date."
